  "chapter": {
    "number": 141,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(142) A Psalm of instruction for David, when he was in the cave, —a Prayer."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I cried to the Lord with my voice; with my voice I made supplication to the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will pour out before him my supplication: I will declare before him my affliction.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When my spirit was fainting within me, then you knew my paths; in the very way wherein I was walking, they hid a snare for me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I looked on my right hand, and behold, for there was none that noticed me; refuge failed me; and there was none that cared for my soul.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I cried to you, O Lord, and said, You are my hope, my portion in the land of the living.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Attend to my supplication, for I am brought very low; deliver me from them that persecute me; for they are stronger than I.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Bring my soul out of prison, that I may give thanks to your name, O Lord; the righteous shall wait for me, until you recompense me.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
